{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.total_unchanged_by_zero_weight_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.total_unchanged_by_zero_weight_block","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L190-L196","doc":"The cost total therefore never sees a zero-weight block: dropping it from\nthe sum changes nothing. Stated for a two-block split, which is the shape at\n`n = 3` once `y_(1³) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.zero_weight_block_contributes_nothing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.zero_weight_block_contributes_nothing","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L175-L188","doc":"**The `(1³)` column is structurally zero, not numerically small.**\n\nA block whose Markov weight vanishes contributes nothing to `t_λ = y_λ·(…)`\nwhatever its characters are. Under convention D `y_(1³) = 0` — that vanishing\nIS convention D (the direction used here, D ⟹ vanish, is\n`FibreDimensionForcesTL.threeRow_eq_zero_of_jones_ocneanu`, or\n`ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_of_three_rows` for general `n`; the converse\nthat makes it an \"IS\" is `markovWeights_eq_jones_of_threeRow_eq_zero`, which also\nneeds `hfaith : y_(2,1) ≠ 0`) — so the alternating block's absence from the cost\nvector is\nthe convention, and a reader seeing a zero column should not look for a bug. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.conventionD_weights_normalise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.conventionD_weights_normalise","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L162-L171","doc":"**`y_(3) + 2·y_(2,1) = 1`** for the convention-D Markov weights at `n = 3`.\n\n`tr_M(1) = ∑_λ y_λ·dim_λ` with dimensions `1, 2, 1`, and `y_(1³) = 0` under\nconvention D, so the identity to check is exactly this one. Proved as an\nalgebraic identity in `q`, valid wherever `q² + 1 ≠ 0` — no numerics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.char_letterPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.char_letterPair","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L138-L158","doc":"**The expansion that makes `χ_λ` of a letter computable.**\n\nA letter is `σ + c·1` — a braid generator only when `c = 0`. For two letters,\n\n    χ((a + c_a·1)(b + c_b·1)) = χ(ab) + c_b·χ(a) + c_a·χ(b) + c_a·c_b·χ(1)\n\nso every term is a character of a braid word of length ≤ 2 (and `χ(1) = dim`).\n`χ` is any linear functional; being a trace is not needed, only linearity.\n\nThis is the identity the block-cost probe's `[A1]` cross-check validated\nagainst an independent trace engine, agreeing to `2.6e-50`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.separation_independent_kernel_is_blind_on_the_measured_transposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.separation_independent_kernel_is_blind_on_the_measured_transposition","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L111-L132","doc":"**The converse to `pairSum_not_perm_invariant`, on the case the probe\nmeasured.**\n\nA kernel that ignores the separation and is symmetric in its two letters gives\nthe SAME value on the transposition where a separation-dependent kernel gives\ndifferent values. So the escape from the letter-sum exclusion is the separation\ndependence specifically — a pair kernel is not enough on its own.\n\nStated as the concrete instance the probe's control measured rather than as a\ngeneral permutation theorem: the general statement needs an induction over\n`List.Perm` that this file does not carry, and claiming it here would be\nasserting more than is proved. The instance is the one that matters, because\n`[0,1,2] ↦ [1,0,2]` is exactly the reordering that separates `σ₁σ₀` from\n`σ₀σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.headPairs_separation_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.headPairs_separation_independent","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L97-L109","doc":"**A separation-independent kernel makes `headPairs` a plain letter sum.**\n\nWith `K x y d = J x y`, the separation argument is never read, so the head's\ncontribution is `∑_{y ∈ ys} J x y` — a sum over the later letters with no\npositional information in it at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.pairSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.pairSum","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L92-L95","doc":"Sum over ordered pairs with a separation-aware kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.headPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.headPairs","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ECatProbeAssertions.lean#L86-L90","doc":"Pairs of a head letter with each later letter, carrying the separation.\nMirrors `ECatBlockDecomposition.headPairs`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}